Bill Wright (wrigb104) is listed in batting slots 1 and 8 and as the starter in
both center field and right field. Nashville carried a second Wright, Henry
Wright (wrigh102), who played for the team in 1934, including the left field
appearance in game 2 the day before. Bill Wright led off in center field in
both games the day before. The slot 8 start record, bline, and the right
field dline are reassigned to Henry Wright; Bill keeps slot 1 in center field.
This is the most likely reading of two different Wrights merged into one ID,
not a confirmed identification.

